Chapter 27 – Part 5
Namie drove.
The city blurred into signals and glass. Seiji’s bruise sat in the back of her mind like a bill. The girl sat in front of it. Nightstar sat in the passenger seat even after the seat was empty.
“He did it again,” she told the windshield. “Why does he make me feel this way.”
Beautiful. Miss Namie. Dinner. A range. Maybe.
She did not like men who asked. She liked control. She liked Seiji’s name and the way a company door closed. This was not that. This was a foreigner with two sugars and a voice that made her last name feel optional.
She turned the radio up so she would not answer herself.

Curtis walked the other way.
The coffee taste went flat.
“That was an ugly thing of me to do. I don’t normally play with hearts like that.” He exhaled through his teeth. “But it dropped her trail off me.”
The date had been a flare. Pink ears. A maybe. A woman scanning his mouth instead of his morning. Far from Mikado’s kettle. Far from a reconstructed neck.
He did not like the trick. Justice would have called it cruel and then done it cleaner. Curtis called it what it was and kept walking.
School later. Harmless mask. Anri with half a loop. Masaomi with questions. A girl already found.
On two different roads, the same minute split.
Namie Yagiri wondered why her chest had filed him.
Curtis Nightstar wondered what kind of man used a maybe
as camouflage —
and went toward the bell anyway,
because Mika Harima
was not going back on a table.